                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm afraid to say that this \"game\" is a one-trick pony.  The developers have created a series of very small mesh terrains, populated them with stock houses and trees, and loaded in a set of stock airplane models which don't even animate (no elevons/aileron movement when you fly).  The 'mesh' is tiny, maybe a few 2Km on a side, so you're always in sight of the edge of the world, and can see the skybox beyond!   \n\nThe music is a series of wierd jazzy / dancy / poppy stuff that wouldn't be out of place as hold music.   It's okay, I guess, but doesn't really fit with the \"relaxed flying experience\" the game promises.\n\nThe keyboard controls are weird.. while W and S are pitch down and up, as you'd expect, A and D are the rudders, and turning like a plane is achieved by Q and E which doesn't feel natural at all... \n\nAll of the above is just a distraction from the main reason why you should avoid the game: It's broken.   As of writing this only two of the levels work, and both of them are basically exactly the same game: fly around and hit strange balls hovering in the air.   That is, of course, when the game works.  When it was released onto Steam, it wouldn't even run, and kept throwing an error \"Executable not found\"!\n\nThe game feels like a bunch of stock models, put above a few terrains generated in a terrain mesh tool.  The flight model is not brilliant, and the ball-collecting mechanic just isn't fun after you've done it for 30 minutes or more....   \n\nSorry, but it's a 'no' from me.  This'll be the first game I ask for a refund, it's just too broken.  It needs a LOT of work, and a lot of fixing.  Plus some interaction from the developers would be a good start!",
                        "timestamp_created": 1517922001,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1517922001,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 8,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6711623668670654,
                        "comment_count": 2,
